'' RUN: the cleanups a GOTO runs come from WHERE its label is, not from a depth. A jump
'' to a label in its own IF arm destroyed the arm's locals at the jump and again at the
'' end of the arm (the label pre-scan did not know an arm is a scope) -- a double free
'' for a type owning memory; a jump into a SIBLING scope ran nothing for the one it left;
'' a BACKWARD jump ran nothing for what was defined after its label. Output identical to
'' fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/goto-cleanup.bas -o tests/codegen/gotocleanup.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/gotocleanup.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +6[lbl1]-6[end]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [lbl2 50]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [lbl2 50]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: val= 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: val= 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: val= 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +3-3[lbl4][end]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +0-0+1-1+2-2[out]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [d1][d2][d3][out]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: survived
